title: "Seismic Precursors of LLM Degradation: LRD/QO3/FIO Bridge"
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-01-04"

authors:
  - family-names: Chechelnitsky
    given-names: Igor
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4607-1946"
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher, Ashkelon, Israel"

abstract: >-
  Minimal reproducible demo applying fractal/seismic methodology 
  (Long-Range Dependence, Hurst exponent, QO3/FIO framework) to detect 
  early-warning signals of degradation in long-form LLM generation.
  Token-level entropy and Hurst exponent can predict repetition collapse
  300-1200 tokens before visible degradation.

keywords:
  - long-range dependence
  - LRD
  - Hurst exponent
  - fractal
  - LLM
  - large language model
  - telemetry
  - early warning
  - regime detection
  - QO3
  - FIO
  - test-time compute

